  "description": "Synthetic semantic cases for evaluating an AI provider (§96, §97).\n\nEvery document here is invented. No real manuscript, thesis or customer content appears in this repository, and none ever should: a benchmark corpus is committed, shared and copied, which is the opposite of what unpublished research needs.\n\nExpectations are structural, never textual. An LLM's prose is not byte-deterministic, so asserting on wording would make the suite fail for reasons that have nothing to do with whether the assessment was right. What is asserted is the assessment, the evidence sufficiency, whether human review is required, and which nodes may legitimately be cited.",
